    io-pgtable-dart.c by way of ../m1-sound/kernel/pd_dart_fixed.cpp:
    Copyright (C) 2021 The Asahi Linux Contributors
    based on arm-smmu.c and arm-smmu-v3.c, Copyright (C) 2013, 2015 ARM Limited,
    exynos-iommu.c, Copyright (c) 2011,2016 Samsung Electronics Co., Ltd., and
    io-pgtable-arm, Copyright (C) 2014 ARM Limited
  kernel/pd_soc.cpp, .h (GPL-2.0-only OR MIT): copies of ../m1-touchbar/kernel/pd_soc.*
    (PMGR after m1n1 src/pmgr.c and Linux drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c,
    Copyright The Asahi Linux Contributors)
  kernel/PDAppleAVD.cpp (GPL-2.0): the platform side; register addresses and interrupt
    numbers as in arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8103.dtsi (GPL-2.0+ OR MIT, Copyright The
    Asahi Linux Contributors) and the Apple device tree of the machine

Firmware: the decoder's Cortex-M3 runs the firmware of https://github.com/aurora-silicon/avd-fw
(MIT, Copyright The Asahi Linux Contributors; Arch package avd-fw 0.1-1, image
apple/avd-fw-v2-t0.bin for T8103). It is not part of this repository: the image is taken from
the machine's Linux installation into private/firmware/apple/ and staged per boot.

Userland (MIT unless a file says otherwise): include/pdavd/pdavd.h, pdavd_ioctl.h,
user/ (libpdavd, pdavd-replay), host-test/, tools/, guest/, the Nix recipes.

ffmpeg/0001-pdavd-hwaccel.patch is a patch to FFmpeg 8.1.2 and is under FFmpeg's licence
(LGPL-2.1-or-later). libavcodec/pdavd_h264.c, pdavd_hevc.c and pdavd_vp9.c in it are derived
from the V4L2 request API hwaccels of Jonas Karlman's FFmpeg branch
(github.com/Kwiboo/FFmpeg, v4l2-request-n8.0.1: libavcodec/v4l2_request_h264.c,
v4l2_request_hevc.c, v4l2_request_vp9.c; LGPL-2.1-or-later).

Codecs involved (for whoever assesses patents; nothing here was held back for them):
H.264/AVC, H.265/HEVC, VP9 (the hardware of T8103 has no AV1).
